Gemmi
-----

FastSASA uses Gemmi headers for native mmCIF parsing and writing.

Gemmi is distributed under the Mozilla Public License Version 2.0. The full
license text is kept in `licenses/Gemmi-MPL-2.0.txt` in FastSASA release
packages and `third-party/gemmi/LICENSE.txt` in the development checkout. It
must be included with source and binary redistributions that contain
Gemmi-covered material.

Gemmi bundles small third-party header-only components. Their notices are kept
in the corresponding source headers under `third-party/gemmi/include/gemmi`
and in `third-party/gemmi/include/gemmi/third_party/tao/LICENSE`. Release
packages also ship summary notice files under `licenses/`, including
`Gemmi-third-party-notices.txt` and `TAO-PEGTL-MIT.txt`.

volk
----

FastSASA vendors the volk Vulkan meta-loader (https://github.com/zeux/volk) to
load the Vulkan runtime dynamically. volk is distributed under the MIT
license; the full text is kept in `licenses/volk-MIT.md` in FastSASA release
packages and `third-party/volk/LICENSE.md` in the development checkout.

xdrfile (XTC reader)
--------------------

`third-party/xdrfile/` vendors the xdrfile library (Copyright (c) 2009-2014,
Erik Lindahl & David van der Spoel; BSD 2-Clause License) as distributed with
MDTraj, for the built-in XTC reader. It includes a modified version of the Sun
XDR routines with Sun's original legend. The full texts are in
`licenses/xdrfile-BSD-2-Clause.txt` and `third-party/xdrfile/LICENSE.txt`.
FastSASA adds one accessor, `xdrfile_get_fp()`, and bounds checks that reject
corrupt frames; nothing else is changed.

Validation fixtures
-------------------

The PDB/mmCIF files in `tests/data/` are FreeSASA's test fixtures (see the
FreeSASA section above); the structures themselves are public PDB entries.
`tests/data/1ubq_5frames.*` and `tests/data/1ubq_4atoms.*` are small
FastSASA-generated XTC/DCD trajectories derived from 1UBQ.
Keep their original metadata intact when redistributing source archives.

